## 4. Run: port mapping 8086→8080, named volume, env configuration, restart policy
$ docker volume create ccrp-demo-data
ccrp-demo-data
$ docker run -d --name ccrp-demo -p 8086:8080 -e APP_OFFICER_PASSWORD=******** -e APP_ENVIRONMENT=docker -v ccrp-demo-data:/var/lib/ccrp --restart unless-stopped sanad-ccrp:1.2.0-SNAPSHOT
a42d8056daf3459b9e58cbc9b6c7c85d09ae5de4cf91dfd3d527ffa6dc1ec224
health: healthy
$ docker ps --filter name=ccrp-demo --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}'
NAMES       IMAGE                       STATUS                    PORTS
ccrp-demo   sanad-ccrp:1.2.0-SNAPSHOT   Up 12 seconds (healthy)   0.0.0.0:8086->8080/tcp, [::]:8086->8080/tcp

## 5. Use the running container
$ curl -s http://localhost:8086/actuator/health
{"groups":["liveness","readiness"],"status":"UP"}$ curl -s http://localhost:8086/actuator/info | jq -c '{env: .app.environment, version: .build.version, commit: .git.commit.id}'
{"env":"docker","version":"1.2.0-SNAPSHOT","commit":"cda2f5c"}
submitted application → CCR-2026-WETB8V

